  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"20261016.190333\"\n  # The OpenGL-Registry revision pinned by third_party/OpenGL-Registry/src in\n  # Dawn's DEPS. build.sh fails if it no longer matches; update it together\n  # with the sha256 of gl.xml below.\n  opengl_registry_commit: 6af574a14089ccfee87efe230ebcdd8742859813\n\npackage:\n  name: dawn\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  - url: https://github.com/google/dawn/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n    sha256: 7276879eb9b8e510d960f25d203e4f69e62d0b2d63992a2f941b9d1b27518f59\n    patches:\n      - 0001-Link-imported-dependencies-into-the-monolithic-library.patch\n      - 0002-Allow-overriding-the-path-to-khrplatform.h.patch\n  - if: linux\n    then:\n      # The Khronos gl.xml that Dawn's OpenGL loader is generated from, put\n      # where Dawn's DAWN_OPENGL_REGISTRY_DIR expects it.\n      - url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/KhronosGroup/OpenGL-Registry/${{ opengl_registry_commit }}/xml/gl.xml\n        sha256: b9ca2cfa5c676e901c20d34af3407f1687cde0f1336a5ff7a8974d04c7494ad3\n        file_name: gl.xml\n        target_directory: third_party/OpenGL-Registry/src/xml\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  script:\n    file: build\n    env:\n      OPENGL_REGISTRY_COMMIT: ${{ opengl_registry_commit }}\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - cmake\n    - ninja\n    # Used by Dawn's code generators\n    - python >=3.10\n    - jinja2\n  host:\n    - libabseil\n    - spirv-headers\n    - if: not osx\n      then:\n        # Tint's SPIR-V reader uses the private headers in include/spirv-tools-private.\n        # SPIR-V support is only built with the Vulkan backend, not on macOS.\n        # spirv-tools-internal pulls in the matching spirv-tools and, through its\n        # run_exports, pins it to x.x because the internal spvtools::opt C++ API\n        # is not ABI stable.\n        - spirv-tools-internal\n    - if: not osx\n      then:\n        - libvulkan-headers\n        - vulkan-utility-libraries\n    - if: linux\n      then:\n        - libegl-devel\n        - xorg-libx11\n        - xorg-xorgproto\n  ignore_run_exports:\n    # Only the header-only Vulkan::UtilityHeaders target is used, and libEGL\n    # and libX11 are loaded at runtime with dlopen.\n    from_package:\n      - if: not osx\n        then: vulkan-utility-libraries\n      - if: linux\n        then:\n          - libegl-devel\n          - xorg-libx11\n  run:\n    # Dawn loads the Vulkan loader at runtime\n    - if: linux\n      then:\n        - libvulkan-loader\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      lib:\n        - webgpu_dawn\n      include:\n        - webgpu/webgpu.h\n        - dawn/webgpu_cpp.h\n      files:\n        - ${{ \"Library/\" if win }}lib/cmake/Dawn/DawnConfig.cmake\n  - files:\n      recipe:\n        - test/\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n        - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n        - cmake\n        - ninja\n    script:\n      - cmake -S test -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n      - cmake --build build\n      - if: win\n        then: build\\dawn_test.exe\n        else: ./build/dawn_test\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://dawn.googlesource.com/dawn\n  repository: https://github.com/google/dawn\n  documentation: https://dawn.googlesource.com/dawn/+/HEAD/docs/\n  summary: Dawn, a WebGPU implementation\n  description: |\n    Dawn is an open-source and cross-platform implementation of the WebGPU\n    standard. It exposes a C/C++ API that maps almost one-to-one to the\n    WebGPU IDL and can be managed as part of a larger system such as a Web\n    browser. Dawn provides several WebGPU building blocks, including the\n    Tint shader compiler, and backends for D3D11, D3D12, Metal, Vulkan and\n    OpenGL.\n  license: BSD-3-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - hmaarrfk\n",
